From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 18:40:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drm/sun4i: sun60i-dp: Limit the lanes to what the PHY offers

The connector can have fewer than four lanes left for DisplayPort: pin
assignment D keeps two of them for USB3.

Take the lane limit from the bus width of the PHY, as the DesignWare
DisplayPort driver does, so that the modes are checked against the lanes
the connector has left and the link is trained on them.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: four lanes at pin assignment C as before; two
lanes not tested, no sink offering pin assignment D was at hand.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun60i_dp.c | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun60i_dp.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun60i_dp.c
index c548d8032ad0..187347e3d79f 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun60i_dp.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun60i_dp.c
@@ -354,12 +354,16 @@ static int sun60i_dp_read_caps(struct sun60i_dp *dp)
 	return ret;
 }
 
-/* The highest link rate and lane count both ends support */
+/*
+ * The highest link rate and lane count both ends support. The PHY says how
+ * many lanes the connector has left for DisplayPort.
+ */
 static void sun60i_dp_max_link(struct sun60i_dp *dp, unsigned int *rate,
 			       unsigned int *lanes)
 {
 	*rate = sun60i_dp_link_rates[0];
-	*lanes = SUN60I_DP_MAX_LANES;
+	*lanes = min_t(unsigned int, SUN60I_DP_MAX_LANES,
+		       phy_get_bus_width(dp->phy));
 
 	guard(mutex)(&dp->lock);
 
